Photoshop 26.10.0's own 32-bit files for #679's next build batch, saved in one
session by scripts/photoshop-probe/takes_675_679.py (take1, run
20261023T184243Z-0a40f606; receipts in
~/devel/doctored-fixtures/photoshop/takes-675-679/take1). The scene is a 16 x 12
sRGB canvas built from the runner's constant-colour float TIFFs (three f32
samples, macOS sRGB Profile.icc); Photoshop embeds its linear twin,
"sRGB IEC61966-2.1 (Linear RGB Profile)".

layered32.tif: Bottom (0.25, 0.5, 2.0), Background off; Top (4.0, 1.0, 0.125)
duplicated above it and cleared at x >= 8. Saved with layers and transparency,
image compression NONE, layer compression ZIP, byte order IBM, profile embedded.
The layer records are an Lr32 block (count 2) inside tag 37724, whose entries
are written byte-reversed (MIB8, 23rL) in this little-endian file; IFD0 holds
three 32-bit IEEE float samples.

fill_style32.psd: Base (0.25, 0.5, 2.0); Fill, a Solid Color fill layer of RGB
40/40/200 at 100 %; Shadowed (1.0, 1.0, 1.0) cleared outside x in [4, 12),
y in [3, 9), with a Drop Shadow (black, multiply, 75 %, 120 degrees, no global
light, distance 2, spread 0, size 2). Saved with maximize compatibility. The
layer records are an Lr32 block (count 3); the fill is a SoCo record whose
RGBC doubles are 40.00000141561031, 40.00000141561031 and 200.00000327825546
(not the integers asked for: each is f32(c/255)·255, linear light, as every
32-bit descriptor colour is; the stored composite at the Fill reads
0.1568627), and the shadow sits in lfx2 (and lrFX).

photoshop.json holds the run id, each file's sha256 and size, the declared
scene and Photoshop's rows of each file reopened.
core/tests/psd_photoshop_float32_679.rs parses both and opens both layered to
photoshop.json's rows and the scene's constants within 1e-3·|v| + 1e-6.
